---
/**
 * One icon for a share/utility control.
 *
 * ## ⚠️ Why inline SVG and not an icon font or sprite
 *
 * Six marks is not worth a webfont. A font is a render-blocking third-party
 * request on a page with a 1.2 MB budget (`docs/performance-budget.md`), and
 * the strict CSP allows no external stylesheet at all. Inline SVG costs
 * nothing at request time and inherits `currentColor`, so one icon works on
 * the brand-coloured buttons and the outline buttons alike.
 *
 * This is the same reasoning — and the same 24×24 grid — as `SocialLinks.astro`.
 *
 * ## ⚠️ Every icon here is decorative
 *
 * Each one is `aria-hidden` and `focusable="false"`. The accessible name comes
 * from the control's own Bengali `aria-label` / visible text, so a screen reader
 * says "হোয়াটসঅ্যাপে শেয়ার করুন" once — never "whatsapp icon, হোয়াটসঅ্যাপে শেয়ার করুন".
 *
 * ## Provenance and licence
 *
 * - **Brand marks** (`whatsapp`, `facebook`, `x`) — [Simple Icons](https://simpleicons.org), **CC0 1.0**.
 * - **Utility marks** (`link`, `printer`, `card`) — [Heroicons](https://heroicons.com) v2 outline, **MIT**.
 *
 * Both are inlined path data, not dependencies: nothing is added to
 * `package.json`, and there is no runtime fetch. `scripts/verify-share-icons.mjs`
 * asserts both licences and that every icon named by a share control exists.
 */
interface Props {
  /** Which mark to draw. Must be a key of `FILLED` or `STROKED`. */
  name: 'whatsapp' | 'facebook' | 'x' | 'link' | 'printer' | 'card'
  /** Square edge length in px. */
  size?: number
  class?: string
}

const { name, size = 18, class: className } = Astro.props

/** Brand marks — solid glyphs, filled with `currentColor`. Simple Icons, CC0. */
